@startuml
title "As a User, in the Web UI, I want to sort the list of publications\nin my library by title, author, type or ISBN/ISSN." - SD Level 3

skinparam monochrome false
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Futura
skinparam objectFontSize 20
skinparam backgroundColor CornSilk
skinparam objectBackgroundColor WhiteSmoke
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFFE0
skinparam ArrowFontColor #3B4953
skinparam ActivationBackgroundColor black
hidefootbox
autonumber

actor User
participant ":Frontend" as Frontend
participant ":Backend" as Backend

note over Frontend
This diagram assumes that the User has access to My Library
and that the Frontend has discovered the allowed actions
for /my-library.

To view how the User has this OPTION to retrieve and sort
the library, please see
[[pre-condition-diagram/OPTIONS_Before_GET.puml this diagram]]

The Frontend follows the discovered library href and applies
the selected sort criterion instead of using a hardcoded URL.
end note

User -> Frontend : I want to sort the list of publications in my library
activate Frontend

note right of Frontend
Supported values:
- title
- author
- type
- identifier (ISBN/ISSN)
end note

Frontend -> Backend : GET {library href expanded with sort={sort}}\n+ X-User-Id header
activate Backend

ref over Backend
[[rest-sd-ref-diagrams/GET_Sorted_My_Library_SD.puml GET user's library sorted by selected field]]
end ref

Backend --> Frontend : 200 OK\n+ Collection of LibraryItemResponseDTO\n+ _links
deactivate Backend

Frontend --> User : Display sorted library publications
deactivate Frontend

@enduml
